---
import Container from '@labcat/rocketship/components/Container'
import Figure from '@labcat/rocketship/components/Figure'
import Typography from '@labcat/rocketship/components/Typography'
---

<Container size="content" padded>
  <Typography as="article">
    <h1>Figure</h1>
    <p>
      Figures group self-contained content with an optional caption. Use the <code>Figure</code>
      component for images, diagrams, code, or tables that benefit from a semantic
      <code>&lt;figure&gt;</code> and <code>&lt;figcaption&gt;</code>. The caption uses muted text and
      adapts with container queries.
    </p>

    <h2>Figure with image and caption</h2>
    <Figure caption="A raster image with a short descriptive caption.">
      <img
        alt="Abstract geometric pattern representing the Rocketship design system"
        height="240"
        src="https://picsum.photos/seed/rocketship-figure/800/400"
        width="800"
        loading="lazy"
      />
    </Figure>

    <h2>Figure with image, no caption</h2>
    <Figure>
      <img
        alt="Abstract geometric pattern representing the Rocketship design system"
        height="240"
        src="https://picsum.photos/seed/rocketship-figure-nocaption/800/400"
        width="800"
        loading="lazy"
      />
    </Figure>
    <p>This figure has no caption. Use this form for purely decorative or unlabeled media.</p>

    <h2>Figure with rich caption (slot)</h2>
    <Figure>
      <img
        alt="Abstract geometric pattern representing the Rocketship design system"
        height="240"
        src="https://picsum.photos/seed/rocketship-figure-rich/800/400"
        width="800"
        loading="lazy"
      />
      <Fragment slot="caption">
        Fig. 2 — A caption with <em>emphasis</em> and a <a href="https://example.com">link</a>.
      </Fragment>
    </Figure>

    <h2>Figure with table</h2>
    <Figure caption="Table 1 — Illustrative liability caps (demonstration only).">
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th scope="col">Category</th>
            <th scope="col">Cap (demo)</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td>Indirect or consequential loss</td>
            <td>Excluded except where unlawful</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Aggregate cap (commercial users)</td>
            <td>£100 or fees paid in the prior 12 months</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </Figure>

    <h2>Figure inside Typography (prose-native)</h2>
    <p>The same tokens apply when you author raw HTML inside Typography prose:</p>
    <figure>
      <img
        alt="Abstract geometric pattern representing the Rocketship design system"
        height="240"
        src="https://picsum.photos/seed/rocketship-figure-prose/800/400"
        width="800"
        loading="lazy"
      />
      <figcaption>Prose-native figure — styled via the typography mixins.</figcaption>
    </figure>

    <h2>Using the SCSS mixins directly</h2>
    <p>
      Apply the mixins in your own SCSS when you need figure styling outside the component:
    </p>
    <pre><code>@use '@labcat/rocketship/styles/mixins' as *;

.my-figure &#123;
  @include typography-figure;
&#125;

.my-figure figcaption &#123;
  @include typography-figcaption;
&#125;</code></pre>
  </Typography>
</Container>
